### Full flow — run in order (WebStorm / VS Code REST Client)
@base = http://localhost:3000
@owner = juan

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create wallet
POST {{base}}/wallets
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: wallet-{{owner}}-1

{ "owner": "{{owner}}" }

### ACH deposit (stays pending)
# @name deposit
POST {{base}}/wallets/{{owner}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deposit-{{owner}}-1

{ "amount_cents": 10000 }

### Get deposit
GET {{base}}/deposits/{{deposit.response.body.id}}

### Balance: 10000 pending, 0 available
GET {{base}}/wallets/{{owner}}

### Settle the deposit (Stripe webhook)
POST {{base}}/deposits/{{deposit.response.body.id}}/settle
Idempotency-Key: settle-{{deposit.response.body.id}}

### Balance: 10000 available
GET {{base}}/wallets/{{owner}}

### Hold 2500 for a payout
# @name hold
POST {{base}}/wallets/{{owner}}/holds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: hold-{{owner}}-1

{ "amount_cents": 2500, "ttl_seconds": 900 }

### Capture the hold (the payout went out)
POST {{base}}/holds/{{hold.response.body.id}}/capture
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{hold.response.body.id}}

### Retry: same key → same body + header Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{base}}/holds/{{hold.response.body.id}}/capture
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{hold.response.body.id}}

### Second wallet
POST {{base}}/wallets
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: wallet-maria-1

{ "owner": "maria" }

### Transfer juan → maria
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-juan-maria-1

{ "from": "{{owner}}", "to": "maria", "amount_cents": 1000 }

### Overdraw → 422 insufficient_funds
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-juan-maria-2

{ "from": "{{owner}}", "to": "maria", "amount_cents": 99999999 }

### Entry history
GET {{base}}/wallets/{{owner}}/entries?limit=20

### Reconciliation
GET {{base}}/admin/reconciliation
